course: dictionary
lesson: 7234
title: Physiotherapy and the power of context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Physiotherapy is a kind of treatment. It helps people heal and move better, using exercises, stretching and massage, and sometimes heat or cold. It is not medicine, and it is not a magic charm.
explain: Context helps you spot what a word means. «Studies have found that magnetic bracelets don't help pain more than fake ones, while physiotherapy … really can help back pain.» The word while puts two things side by side, so you can see that physiotherapy is the one that really works.
explain: Watch for the short form physio, which means physiotherapy, and a person who does it is a physiotherapist. Read carefully when a text says one thing happened just before another. «Uncle Mo started physiotherapy the same week he bought his magnet bracelet» shows how timing can fool us into thinking the wrong thing helped.
fact: Physiotherapy means treatment that helps people heal and move better.
fact: Physiotherapy uses exercises, stretching, massage and sometimes heat or cold, not medicine.
fact: «Physio» is a short way of saying physiotherapy, and a «physiotherapist» is the trained person who gives it.
fact: People often have physiotherapy after a broken bone, a sports injury or an operation.
fact: «It worked for me» can mislead you: colds often get better in about a week anyway.
exercise: «Physiotherapy» is treatment that helps people heal and move better. What is it mainly made of? | *Exercises, stretching and massage | Pills and medicine | Sitting still in bed all day | Magnet bracelets
exercise: «Studies have found that magnetic bracelets don't help pain more than fake ones, while physiotherapy really can help back pain.» Which treatment really can help back pain? | Fake bracelets | *Physiotherapy | Magnetic bracelets | Waiting for a cold to go away
exercise: «Uncle Mo started physiotherapy the same week he bought his magnet bracelet.» What does this sentence warn you about? | *Believing something worked just because it happened at the same time | Magnets are a kind of medicine | Colds last for a whole month | Physiotherapy always works in one day
test: «Physio» is a short way of saying what? | Physics | Physical education | *Physiotherapy | Photography
test: Which of these is NOT part of physiotherapy as described in the dictionary? | Exercises | *Taking pills | Massage | Stretching
exam: After a broken arm, Priya has physiotherapy «sessions» each week. What does physiotherapy help her do? | Sleep for a whole week | *Heal and move her arm better using exercises | Wear a magnet bracelet | Take medicine to stop the pain
